Subject: [PATCH] feat: add the Readiness Pathway, volunteer stories, and a
 demo seed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the actionable suggestions from the Pod 2 Demo Day feedback
synthesis. docs/POD2_FEEDBACK_RESPONSE.md tracks every piece of feedback to
what answers it, including what deliberately wasn't done.

- Readiness Pathway (/readiness): a public four-tier self-assessment whose
  tiers are the three church types a reviewer named — newly aware; willing
  leadership, unready congregation; ready but directionless — plus an
  "already going" graduation state. This is the answer to "church isn't a
  persona". Readiness is scored as a floor rather than an average
  (src/lib/readiness.ts): a church sits at the earliest gate it hasn't
  cleared, so an enthusiastic congregation that has never met an
  international student is still tier one. Leadership is measured but never
  gates a tier — "you don't have to be a pastor" is a stance the scoring has
  to respect. Only the two ready tiers get a ChurchedIn call-to-action, with
  a unit test pinning that so it can't drift. Runs client-side and persists
  nothing; a church shouldn't need an account to learn it doesn't need one.

- Volunteer stories + activity feed (/stories): a first-person account from
  someone who already hosted, because a hesitant congregation is recruited
  by the volunteers who said yes, not by announcements. Church-scoped by
  default; an author can opt a story onto their church's profile page, where
  it appears with their first name only — enforced in
  listPublicVolunteerStories, the same query-layer rule first-visit rides
  use. Alongside it an activity feed derived from existing data
  (src/lib/churchActivity.ts) so a church space never looks abandoned.
  Mentor connections and rides are deliberately not feed sources: both are
  one-to-one relationships behind an accept step. Authorship is limited to
  volunteers and leaders — student stories need their own consent design.

- Landing page: lead with the three things a group chat structurally can't
  do (auto-waitlists, a privacy-gated friend directory, a per-church space
  with a join code), framed as "keep your WhatsApp group" rather than asking
  anyone to switch, plus a route into the pathway for churches that aren't
  ready. Extracted PublicHeader so the landing and readiness pages share it.

- npm run db:seed (prisma/seed.ts): a demo church with 10 people and 3
  gatherings — one past, one deliberately over capacity so the waitlist is
  real, one with room. Re-runnable, and it refuses to touch a church that
  isn't unmistakably its own, so a join-code collision can't wipe real data.

- /stories is added to the proxy matcher: it has a loading.tsx, so without
  that an anonymous request gets a 200 and a shell with a client-side
  redirect instead of a clean bounce to /login.

The ISM-in-a-box gap analysis has its framework and one-sentence gap
statement written, but its comparison table is deliberately left unfilled —
nobody has read the source material yet, and every claim about what it
contains is marked UNVERIFIED rather than guessed at.

