+# ISM-in-a-box gap analysis
+
+**Status: framework complete, empirical claims unverified.**
+Owner: Preston & Ranjita · Prepared for the next Joyce/Aaron check-in
+
+This is Aaron's explicit ask from Ideation Demo Day: what does ISM-in-a-box
+already cover, what remains uncovered, and can we state our gap in one
+sentence. Thanh raised the same question about IFI's existing toolkit.
+
+Read the honesty note before using any of this in a room with Aaron.
+
+---
+
+## The one-sentence gap
+
+> **ISM-in-a-box helps a church design a ministry. The Playbook Exchange
+> helps churches copy what already worked at another church.**
+
+The distinction we're claiming is **prescriptive vs. peer-produced**: a
+curriculum is authored once by people with expertise and handed down, while an
+exchange is written continuously by practitioners and passed sideways. If that
+distinction turns out not to hold — if ISM-in-a-box already contains a living
+library of church-contributed practice — the Playbook Exchange has no reason
+to exist as a separate thing and should be folded into the Readiness Pathway
+as content rather than built as a product.
+
+We should be willing to say that out loud at the check-in.
+
+---
+
+## Honesty note — read before the check-in
+
+Nobody on the pod has done a page-by-page review of ISM-in-a-box or of IFI's
+existing toolkit. The framework below is complete and the questions are the
+right ones, but **every claim about what those resources contain is currently
+an assumption**, marked `[UNVERIFIED]`.
+
+Walking into a check-in with a filled-in comparison table we guessed at is
+worse than walking in with the empty one and a plan, because Aaron will know
+which cells we made up. The table below is deliberately left unfilled.
+
+**Before the check-in, someone has to actually read the source material.**
+That is a two-hour job, not a research project:
+
+1. Get the current ISM-in-a-box materials (ask Joyce — she can point us at the
+   canonical version rather than whatever is findable online).
+2. Get IFI's existing toolkit, which Thanh referenced as a separate overlap
+   risk from ISM-in-a-box. Confirm whether they're the same artifact.
+3. Fill in the table, one row per section of the actual table of contents.
+4. Re-check whether the one-sentence gap above survives contact with it.
+
+---
+
+## Comparison framework
+
+For each capability a church needs, mark whether ISM-in-a-box covers it, and
+whether what we're building duplicates it or extends it.
+
+| Capability a church needs | ISM-in-a-box | IFI toolkit | Us | Verdict |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Theology / motivation for welcoming international students | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Out of scope — deliberately | — |
+| Assessing whether this church is ready to start | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Readiness Pathway (`/readiness`) | — |
+| Designing a ministry from scratch (structure, roles, calendar) | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Out of scope — assumed covered | — |
+| Recruiting volunteers from a hesitant congregation | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Volunteer stories (`/stories`) | — |
+| Field-tested practice from other, comparable churches | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Playbook Exchange (unbuilt) | — |
+| Day-to-day coordination: gatherings, headcounts, waitlists | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | ChurchedIn (built) | — |
+| Student-initiated one-to-one connections, safely gated | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | ChurchedIn friend directory (built) | — |
+| Year-two sustainability and volunteer handoff | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Partially — see gap below | — |
+| Cross-denominational coordination | `[UNVERIFIED]` | `[UNVERIFIED]` | Deferred (Campus Coordination Network) | — |
+
+Verdict column values: **duplicate** (stop building), **extend** (keep, and
+say what it adds), **genuine gap** (keep, and lead with it).
+
+## Our strongest a-priori claim
+
+Whatever ISM-in-a-box contains, it is a document, and a document cannot:
+
+- hold a live headcount, or promote someone off a waitlist when a family drops
+  out;
+- withhold a student's email address until both people have agreed to connect;
+- survive the volunteer who set it up moving away.
+
+That is the same argument the landing page now makes against WhatsApp
+(`src/app/BeyondGroupChat.tsx`), and it applies to a curriculum just as much:
+**a curriculum tells a church what to do; it doesn't hold the state of the
+church doing it.** This claim needs no verification of ISM-in-a-box's contents
+to be true, which makes it the safest thing to lead with if the reading
+doesn't happen in time.
+
+## What this analysis does not resolve
+
+Two reviewers (R. Dong, Danielle, Jonathan on the follow-up pipeline;
+Aaron on year two) raised sustainability, and honestly neither ISM-in-a-box
+nor anything we've built answers it yet. A church that hosts three dinners in
+September and nothing in February has not been failed by a lack of tooling or
+a lack of curriculum. We should not claim this as a gap we fill.
