+/**
+ * A short first-person account from a volunteer about hosting — "we had four
+ * students over and nobody wanted to leave". Demo Day feedback (Thanh) was
+ * that volunteer supply and motivation is the real constraint, and that the
+ * people best placed to recruit a hesitant congregation are the volunteers
+ * who already said yes. So this is a recruiting surface, not a social feed:
+ * church-scoped by default, appears on /stories alongside a derived activity
+ * feed, and optionally (`sharePublicly`) on the church's profile page. That
+ * page is cross-tenant readable (any signed-in user can load any church's
+ * profile — that's what /discover is for), so `sharePublicly` means "outside
+ * my church", not "on the open internet": a student deciding which church to
+ * visit is exactly who a host's story needs to reach.
+ *
+ * Authorship is limited to VOLUNTEER and CHURCH_ADMIN members, enforced in
+ * src/lib/actions/stories.ts. Students are deliberately excluded for now:
+ * a student's account of being welcomed is arguably the most persuasive
+ * thing on the platform, but it's also the one most likely to expose a
+ * vulnerable person to readers outside their own church, and it needs its
+ * own consent design before it goes anywhere near `sharePublicly`.
+ *
+ * When a story IS shared beyond the church, only the author's first name goes
+ * with it — the same rule listOpenRideRequestsForChurch applies to
+ * FIRST_VISIT rides, enforced the same way (at the query layer, in
+ * listPublicVolunteerStories, not left to each page to remember).
+ */
+model VolunteerStory {
+  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
+  body          String
+  sharePublicly Boolean  @default(false)
+  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())
+
+  churchId String
+  church   Church @relation(fields: [churchId], references: [id])
+  authorId String
+  author   User   @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])
+
+  // Every read of this table is "this church's stories, newest first" — the
+  // in-app feed, the church profile page, and the activity feed all want
+  // exactly that order.
+  @@index([churchId, createdAt])
 }
 
